[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3561811819","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112989#issuecomment-3561811819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112989","id":3561811819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UTO9r","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-21T07:37:08Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T07:38:51Z","body":"Yes, a lot of storage textures in Godot use half floats and load them using imageLoad in compute shaders without any prior checks to see if that's actually supported. \r\n\r\nMaking [this value in the shader translator](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/drivers/d3d12/rendering_shader_container_d3d12.cpp#L285) true might help, but I found some shaders that use both `imageLoad` and `imageStore` on the same half float storage texture, so it wouldn't work in those cases.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"http